    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.35) and **Jackson Merrill** (62.07). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** represents our most reliable engine against Elder, bolstered by a strong 0.371 xwOBA and favorable alignment in the three-hole. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** provides a massive boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage against Nola; while we track stolen bases as our scarcest commodity, his ability to contribute across the board makes him a tier-one play despite the moderate skill of the opposing arm. **Kyle Tucker** (61.08) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (61.04) round out our premier options, with the latter benefiting significantly from a platoon-advantage matchup against the right-handed Bachar.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Coby Mayo** (48.16) for a spot in the starting lineup. **Coby Mayo** showed promise with a park-factor boost of +7%, but he was ultimately squeezed out by the more consistent efficiency profiles of **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung**. We are keeping a close watch on **Gunnar Henderson** (50.92); despite his elite status, his score is suppressed today by a tough matchup against Early and a negative dynamic platoon split, though his positioning in the two-hole keeps him firmly in the lineup. Conversely, we are avoiding **Brayan Rocchio** (35.70), who falls well below our 40-point floor due to a poor lineup spot and a difficult outing against Schlittler. Finally, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving a gap in our speed-focused outfield strategy that we must navigate with current depth options like **Miguel Andujar** and **Dominic Smith**.",
